{
  "_comment": [
    "Named practice sections for the loop (docs/04 §5, P18).",
    "",
    "Keyed by catalog id and merged into `teaching.sections` by the build, because an item's",
    "notes arrive through three different pipelines — authored ABC, imported MusicXML and the",
    "PDMX quarry — and one file is better than three mechanisms.",
    "",
    "`fromBar`/`toBar` are **1-based positions in the printed score**: bar 1 is the first",
    "printed bar, a pickup included. That is what a player counts and what the model's",
    "`sourceMeasureIndex` counts from, so the Score screen can turn a section into a loop",
    "without knowing anything about repeats.",
    "",
    "Every range here was read off the file — repeat marks, double barlines and the first note",
    "of each bar — rather than from what the piece is usually shaped like. validate.py checks",
    "each one lies inside the piece's printed bar count from the render report."
  ],
